<title>BOLIVIA: SOCCER-BRAZIL BEAT MEXICO 3-2 IN COPA AMERICA.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZIL BEAT MEXICO 3-2 IN COPA AMERICA.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CRUZ, Bolivia 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil beat Mexico</p>
<p>3-2 (halftime 0-2) in a Copa America first round group C match</p>
<p>on Monday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Brazil - Aldair (48th minute), Romario (62), Leonardo (80)</p>
<p>Mexico - Luis Hernandez (14, 32)</p>
<p>Attendance: 35,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Brazil	  2  2  0  0  8  2  6</p>
<p> Colombia	2  1  0  1  5  3  3</p>
<p> Mexico	  2  0  0  2  4  4  3</p>
<p> Costa Rica    2  0  0  2  1  9  0</p>
<p>Note: top two teams in each group plus the two</p>
<p>third-placed teams with the best records qualify for the</p>
<p>quarter-finals. Brazil already qualified.</p>
<p>Next games: June 19 - Costa Rica v Mexico, Brazil v</p>
<p>Colombia.</p>
</text>
